  "reason": "Evidence: The top three experiments (config_008: 0.725, config_019: 0.721, config_013: 0.713) all use scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation, with weighted fusion and imagenet_vit_l as the best combination. However, we have not yet tested whether transformer aggregation is truly necessary versus simpler avgpool when paired with the best RNA encoder and image encoder. This experiment (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates the aggregation variable while holding all other components at their best-known settings. If avgpool matches transformer (~0.725), it confirms the architecture is robust and frees us to explore other dimensions (e.g., singleprofile, different encoders) in the remaining 4 experiments. If avgpool is significantly worse, it confirms transformer is a critical component and we should focus remaining budget on fusion/image-encoder refinements around the transformer backbone. This is the highest-information experiment because it reduces uncertainty on a key architectural choice with a clean one-variable comparison."
